<title>UK: TEPCO plans $1.0 bln 10-year bond-dealers.</title>
<headline>TEPCO plans $1.0 bln 10-year bond-dealers.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-01-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Tokyo Electric Power Co Inc (TEPCO) was expected to launch a $1.0 billion 10-year bond next week, syndicate managers said on Friday.</p>
<p>Spread talk was around 32 basis points over U.S. Treasury notes, they said. Goldman Sachs was tipped as lead manager.</p>
<p>&quot;A TEPCO 10-year dollar jumbo will surface next week, and there was talk they were also looking at marks,&quot; said a syndicate manager at a Japanese bank in London.</p>
<p>TEPCO was last in the market in August when it launched a 4.0 billion French franc 10-year bond at 15 b.p. over OATs.</p>
<p>-- Aline van Duyn, London Newsroom +44 171 542 7748</p>
